      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "Four stores with different jobs",
        "session.db is the audit trail and also hosts the appliance-state and runbook tables, with FTS5 over every turn",
        "skills.db holds seed and self-authored procedures and feeds the compact index in each prompt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "The appliance state machine and runbook tables, which also live in session.db but are shown where they are used",
        "Connected but out of scope: Email gateway, Cron scheduler, CLI REPL, Claude API, Context compressor, Session FSM"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What it guarantees",
      "items": [
        "Every session, turn, tool call, approval, alert, and expiry is persisted, with FTS5 search across the whole conversation history."
      ]
    }
  ]
